# dark-versus-lit combat narration matrix -- internal/hooks dispatchCritAndMessaging
# Each cell drives the REAL production seam (dispatchCritAndMessaging, including
# replaceDarknessMessages and the verbosity drain) with a one-variant-per-outcome
# label fixture, so the golden records WHICH LINE won, not authored prose.
# columns: atk sight | def sight | outcome | reader => text
# PRE-FLIP (today): any cell where a participant's OWN sight isn't 'full' shows one
# of the twelve hardcoded dark sentences on THAT participant's line, replacing the
# AUTHORED pool line. The spectator line is never substituted by replaceDarknessMessages
# (it only ever touched MessagesToSource/MessagesToTarget, never MessagesToSourceRoom,
# and M4d PR 2 deleted it regardless) -- but under the graded lighting arc's window
# model, no vision condition restores SightFull in a truly dark room, so the spectator's
# own darkness gates their visual room line off in every cell, same as an unsighted
# bystander, and they read the audible fallback instead (lighting plan 5c: the fallback
# follows sight, not the nightvision flag).

atk=full|def=full|hit|attacker => AUTHORED|hit|actor.
atk=full|def=full|hit|defender => AUTHORED|hit|actee.
atk=full|def=full|hit|spectator => You hear fighting close by.
atk=full|def=full|crit|attacker => AUTHORED|crit|actor.
